commit d8d2ae6d08adf096d700e5e6a73d3882cf92c773
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 10:18:14 2026 +1100

    agent: Import the resource cache only for L2 agents
    
    neutron.agent.rpc imports the resource cache and registry, which load
    every object and DB model, though only L2 agents use them, and
    stdattrs_common imports standard_attr for one function. Import them when
    used, spell RESOURCE_TYPES out, and test the DHCP, L3 and metadata
    agents.
    
    With neutron-lib's "Load the DB API only for DB users", "db: Import the
    DB API inside the functions using it" and "ovn: Keep server-only imports
    out of the OVN agent", the probe shows those agents down from 119, 119
    and 115MB to 103, 102 and 99MB, without the DB API or pecan; without the
    neutron-lib change, 10 to 12MB.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for the neutron changes that keep the DB API out of
    the neutron agents, as three patches grouped by the agents they free.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    
    Change-Id: Ibce838389c8edb25fdc6affbe3dd1c517d6d6d53
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

